# hooks and gates

**Read [`memory/hooks-and-gates.md`](../memory/hooks-and-gates.md) before going further.** This rule exists to
fire on the topic and send you there; the knowledge itself lives in one place, not two.

**Why it is worth the read:** The one check fails OPEN, and a hook that never loaded looks exactly like a hook that correctly allowed the commit. Nothing in the source says which of those you are looking at.

## Before you touch anything

- Run `node hooks/status.js` and read "Last commit check": it is written only when the check runs on a commit, so an empty one after commits means the hook is not loaded.
- Restart the host before debugging a hook that does not fire. Hook config is read at startup.
- Only the commit is refused. Do not add a block to an edit or to a turn end; add a reminder in `gates.reminders`.
- Never match a raw absolute `file_path`. Relativise against `cwd` first -- `toProjectPath` in `hooks/lib/gates.js`.

